30,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we struggle with balance. Last year we were too separate, but a shared house leaves no room for privacy. We need a middle ground.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Shizue,,I've found that renting a whole building makes the bill much fairer and simpler to divide than booking separate rooms.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Minato,,The island house sounds scary because of the cold water and only one bathroom. The inn has a strict schedule and we all sleep together.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The island trip takes too much time just to get there and back. The spa valley is much closer by train.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The island houses are very cheap, but the valley inn is a fixed price including meals, which is much easier to budget for.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Minato, if the inn's shared room is too much, maybe the city is better? But @Jonathan says the valley is efficient.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, if the valley inn is a fixed rate, it avoids the confusion of who owes what for every single meal.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Minato,,I don't like the idea of everyone in one room on futons. I might not sleep well.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"The city is the most flexible for movement, but the spa valley is a good compromise on travel time.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Midori,,The city beds are quite expensive and the costs are unpredictable since meals are extra.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we go to the city, we risk being too disconnected again. The spa town allows us to be together but still have public spaces.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Shizue,,A single bill for a house or an all-in inn rate is definitely the most peaceful way to handle money.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Minato,,Is there any way to have a private room in the spa town? Or maybe the city is safer for my sleep.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,The city's transport is seamless. No waiting for hourly buses or ferries. It's the least stressful for the schedule.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Midori,,I'm leaning toward the valley inn because the total cost is clear from the start.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,Let's consider the options. The island is too restrictive and slow. The city is too fragmented. The spa town seems the most balanced.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. The all-in rate at the inn would prevent any quiet resentment over money.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm still worried about the futons, but the bathroom situation at the island house sounds even worse.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"As long as we aren't wasting two days on a ferry, I can support the spa town.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Midori,,It sounds like the Hot Spring Town is the best fit for everyone's needs.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
